IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sazwt-law`
IMPORT `sazwt-seat`

-- Tests for SAZV § 5(2), § 6(1) and § 12 under both readings, and the citation test. Expected values are written from the deposited German text
-- (sazv-5, sazv-6, sazv-12, their *-before-2025 transcriptions, the 2025 gazette and the preambles), not from this encoding's output.
-- P is `as printed`; V is `if the 2025 amendment is void`.
-- Arguments to `the working week of a soldier with`: part-time reduction in percent, service reasons call for a departure, service reasons stand against an individual distribution.
-- Arguments to `the working day of a soldier with`: hours fixed, service reasons require more than 13 hours, area, what has happened, excessive unforeseeable workload, continuity must be ensured.
-- Arguments to `the calendar month of a soldier with`: hours on call, hours actually called on, hours blocked by compelling service reasons, working-time arrangement.

§ `§ 5(2) sentences 1 and 2: the days`

-- Full time, no service reasons: "in der Regel auf Montag bis Freitag" under both readings.
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `Monday to Friday`
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `Monday to Friday`
-- Full time, service reasons: as printed "hiervon abgewichen" (any day); before 2025 "auf Montag bis Samstag".
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `any days of the week`
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `Monday to Saturday`
-- Part time reduced by 9 %: "um weniger als 10 Prozent", so the earlier sentence 1 reaches the soldier as it reaches a full-timer.
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working week of a soldier with` 9 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `Monday to Saturday`
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working week of a soldier with` 9 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `Monday to Friday`
-- Part time reduced by exactly 10 %: not "weniger als 10 Prozent", so the earlier § 5(2) does not say; as printed, sentence 1 reaches all part-timers.
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working week of a soldier with` 10 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` 10 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `Monday to Friday`
-- Part time reduced by half, service reasons: as printed any day; before 2025 the text does not reach the soldier.
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` 50 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `any days of the week`
#ASSERT `the days the regular weekly working time may be distributed over under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working week of a soldier with` 50 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 5(2) sentence 1 reaches the soldier under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` 50 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`section 5(2) sentence 1 reaches the soldier under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working week of a soldier with` 50 FALSE FALSE))

§ `§ 5(2) sentence 3: an individual distribution on application`

-- As printed: "kann auf Antrag genehmigt werden, soweit dienstliche Gründe nicht entgegenstehen".
#ASSERT `an individual distribution over Monday to Friday may be approved on application under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an individual distribution over Monday to Friday may be approved on application under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- It reaches part-timers too: sentence 3 names no group.
#ASSERT `an individual distribution over Monday to Friday may be approved on application under the reading` `as printed` (`the working week of a soldier with` 50 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Before 2025 § 5(2) had two sentences and neither speaks of an application: the text does not answer.
#ASSERT `an individual distribution over Monday to Friday may be approved on application under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an individual distribution over Monday to Friday may be approved on application under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working week of a soldier with` 0 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `§ 6(1): the 13-hour limit`

-- "darf 13 Stunden einschließlich der Pausen nicht überschreiten": 12 and 13 hours are within it under both readings, with no ground needed.
#ASSERT `the regular daily working time fixed for the day is within section 6(1) under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 12 FALSE `another area` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the regular daily working time fixed for the day is within section 6(1) under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 13 FALSE `another area` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the regular daily working time fixed for the day is within section 6(1) under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 13 FALSE `another area` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the regular daily working time fixed for the day is within section 6(1) under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 13.5 FALSE `another area` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE))
-- "wenn dienstliche Gründe dies erfordern" governs both versions: guard duty without service reasons gives no ground under either.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 FALSE `guard, special or orderly duty` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no ground: the 13-hour limit holds`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 FALSE `guard, special or orderly duty` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no ground: the 13-hour limit holds`
#ASSERT NOT (`the regular daily working time fixed for the day is within section 6(1) under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 FALSE `guard, special or orderly duty` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE))

§ `§ 6(1) sentence 3: the grounds, area by area`

-- Guard duty with service reasons: as printed no. 1; before 2025 a named area (old no. 4).
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `guard, special or orderly duty` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 1 as printed: guard, special, orderly or military police duty`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `guard, special or orderly duty` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list names`
-- Military police and close protection: named only in 2025 (no. 1); before 2025 not named, but the list was illustrative, so service reasons suffice.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `military police duty (Feldjägerdienst) or close protection (Personenschutzdienst)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 1 as printed: guard, special, orderly or military police duty`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `military police duty (Feldjägerdienst) or close protection (Personenschutzdienst)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list does not name`
-- Permanent operational tasks (old no. 3), service reasons, no continuity requirement, nothing out of the ordinary: as printed no ground; before 2025 a named area.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no ground: the 13-hour limit holds`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list names`
#ASSERT NOT (`the regular daily working time fixed for the day is within section 6(1) under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the regular daily working time fixed for the day is within section 6(1) under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE)
-- The same tasks where the continuity of the service must be ensured: as printed no. 3 by its general words.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `permanent operational tasks (Dauereinsatzaufgaben)` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 3 as printed: the continuity of the service must be ensured`
-- Other service in a curative medical facility (not nursing or treatment): before 2025 "Dienst in kurativen Sanitätseinrichtungen" names it; as printed letter e names only "Pflege- oder Behandlungsdienste".
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `other service in a curative medical facility` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no ground: the 13-hour limit holds`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `other service in a curative medical facility` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list names`
-- Nursing in a curative facility: named in both.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `nursing or treatment in a curative medical facility` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 3 as printed: an area named under letters a to i`
-- Deployment training: before 2025 "Einsatzausbildung" without limit; as printed only "eintägige Ausbildungs- und Übungsvorhaben" (letter c).
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `deployment training (Einsatzausbildung) other than a one-day project` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no ground: the 13-hour limit holds`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `deployment training (Einsatzausbildung) other than a one-day project` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list names`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `deployment training (Einsatzausbildung) as a one-day training or exercise project` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 3 as printed: an area named under letters a to i`
-- Areas named only in 2025 (letters a "Basisausbildung", d, f, i): as printed named; before 2025 not named, service reasons suffice.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `military air traffic control` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 3 as printed: an area named under letters a to i`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `military air traffic control` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list does not name`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `preparing or running an event of considerable public interest` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 3 as printed: an area named under letters a to i`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `Basisausbildung` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 3 as printed: an area named under letters a to i`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `Basisausbildung` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list does not name`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `operating an airport or a port, firefighting included` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 3 as printed: an area named under letters a to i`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `operating an airport or a port, firefighting included` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list does not name`
-- Letter e reaches nursing or treatment in a rescue service; the earlier no. 5 named only service in curative medical facilities.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `nursing or treatment in a rescue service` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 3 as printed: an area named under letters a to i`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `nursing or treatment in a rescue service` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list does not name`
-- Named in both: a one-day sea voyage (old no. 6, letter g), a long-haul flight (old no. 7, letter h).
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `a one-day sea voyage of a seagoing navy unit` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 3 as printed: an area named under letters a to i`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `a long-haul flight as aircraft crew` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list names`
-- Another area, service reasons, nothing out of the ordinary: as printed no ground; before 2025 service reasons suffice.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `another area` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no ground: the 13-hour limit holds`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `another area` `nothing out of the ordinary` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 before 2025: service reasons, in an area the list does not name`

§ `§ 6(1) sentence 3 no. 2 as printed: extraordinary events and accidents`

-- An accident that leads to an excessive, unforeseeable workload: no. 2, in any area.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `another area` `an accident` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 2 as printed: an extraordinary event or accident`
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `another area` `an extraordinary event` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 2 as printed: an extraordinary event or accident`
-- An accident whose workload is not excessive and unforeseeable: not no. 2.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `another area` `an accident` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `no ground: the 13-hour limit holds`
-- An excessive workload with nothing out of the ordinary behind it: not no. 2.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `another area` `nothing out of the ordinary` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `no ground: the 13-hour limit holds`
-- Guard duty during an accident: the first ground in the text's order is given, no. 1.
#ASSERT `the ground on which the regular daily working time may exceed 13 hours under the reading` `as printed` (`the working day of a soldier with` 14 TRUE `guard, special or orderly duty` `an accident` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `sentence 3 no. 1 as printed: guard, special, orderly or military police duty`

§ `§ 12: compensation for on-call duty`

-- "mehr als 10 Stunden ... ein Achtel der über 10 Stunden hinausgehenden Zeit": the same arithmetic under both readings when nothing is blocked.
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `as printed` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 26 0 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 26 0 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `as printed` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 18 0 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `as printed` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 11 0 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 0.125
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `as printed` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 10 0 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 10 0 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 9 0 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 0
-- § 12(2): eight of 26 on-call hours actually called on are working time; 18 hours of Rufbereitschaft count, so one hour.
#ASSERT `the hours of Rufbereitschaft that count` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 26 8 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 26 8 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 1
-- "soweit nicht zwingende dienstliche Gründe entgegenstehen", as printed only: half an hour blocked of two leaves 1.5; three blocked of two leaves none.
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `as printed` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 26 0 0.5 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 1.5
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 26 0 0.5 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `as printed` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 34 0 3 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `if the 2025 amendment is void` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 34 0 3 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the hours of compensation owed for the month's Rufbereitschaft under the reading` `as printed` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 26 0 2 `fixed working time`) EQUALS 0
-- "innerhalb von zwölf Monaten"; sentences 3 and 4: time off with fixed working time, a credit with flexitime.
#ASSERT `the months within which the compensation must be given` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the form of the compensation` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 26 0 0 `fixed working time`) EQUALS `time off (Dienstbefreiung)`
#ASSERT `the form of the compensation` (`the calendar month of a soldier with` 26 0 0 `flexitime (Gleitzeit)`) EQUALS `a credit to the flexitime account`

§ `Art. 80(1) sentence 3 GG: the 2025 preamble and the power over regular working time`

-- The three instructions rest on § 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 with § 93(2) no. 6.
#ASSERT `the power the instruction rests on` `Art. 5 No. 1: section 5(2)` EQUALS `SG 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 with 93(2) no. 6`
#ASSERT `the power the instruction rests on` `Art. 5 No. 3: section 6(1) sentence 3` EQUALS `SG 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 with 93(2) no. 6`
#ASSERT `the power the instruction rests on` `Art. 5 No. 4: section 12(1) sentence 2` EQUALS `SG 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 with 93(2) no. 6`
-- The 2025 preamble names eight powers; of § 30c(5) it names only "Satz 1 Nummer 2 in Verbindung mit Absatz 4" (bgbl-2025-i-78.txt:38).
#ASSERT count `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2025 amending regulation` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT NOT (`the preamble cites the power` `SG 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 with 93(2) no. 6` `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2025 amending regulation`)
#ASSERT `the preamble cites the power` `SG 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 2 with 30c(4) and 93(2) no. 6` `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2025 amending regulation`
-- It does name § 93(2) no. 6, which names "die regelmäßige Arbeitszeit ... nach § 30c Absatz 5" (sg-93.txt:19): the fact fork F1 turns on.
#ASSERT `the preamble names section 93(2) no. 6 of the Soldiers Act` `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2025 amending regulation`
#ASSERT NOT (`the cited power names section 93(2) no. 6 of the Soldiers Act` `SG 30d(1) sentence 1 with 93(2) no. 8`)
-- The 2022 preamble names § 93(2) nos. 6 and 7 and no part of § 30c; the 2015 preamble names § 30c Absatz 5 as a whole.
#ASSERT count `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2022 amending regulation` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the preamble names section 93(2) no. 6 of the Soldiers Act` `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2022 amending regulation`
#ASSERT NOT (`the preamble cites the power` `SG 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 with 93(2) no. 6` `the powers cited in the preamble of the 2022 amending regulation`)
#ASSERT count `the powers cited in the original preamble of the SAZV` EQUALS 1
-- Controls: a list that holds the needed power tests as cited; the 2015 list does not count as naming § 93(2) no. 6 (it names "§ 93 Absatz 2 Nummer 5", as § 93 was numbered in 2015).
#ASSERT `the preamble cites the power` `SG 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 with 93(2) no. 6` (LIST `SG 30c(5) sentence 1 no. 1 with 93(2) no. 6`, `ArbSiG 38(1)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the preamble names section 93(2) no. 6 of the Soldiers Act` `the powers cited in the original preamble of the SAZV`)
-- Void unless an exception applies; the reading follows.
#ASSERT `the instruction is void for want of citation` `Art. 5 No. 1: section 5(2)` FALSE
#ASSERT `the instruction is void for want of citation` `Art. 5 No. 3: section 6(1) sentence 3` FALSE
#ASSERT `the instruction is void for want of citation` `Art. 5 No. 4: section 12(1) sentence 2` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the instruction is void for want of citation` `Art. 5 No. 3: section 6(1) sentence 3` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the reading to apply to the instruction` `Art. 5 No. 4: section 12(1) sentence 2` FALSE EQUALS `if the 2025 amendment is void`
#ASSERT `the reading to apply to the instruction` `Art. 5 No. 4: section 12(1) sentence 2` TRUE EQUALS `as printed`
